msgid "What is Base?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:21
msgid ""
"Base is a framework for rapidly creating high quality node.js "
"applications, using plugins like building blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:23
msgid "Guiding principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:25
msgid "The core team follows these principles to help guide API decisions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:27
msgid ""
"**Compact API surface**: The smaller the API surface, the easier the "
"library will be to learn and use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:28
msgid ""
"**Easy to extend**: Implementors can use any npm package, and write "
"plugins in pure JavaScript. If you're building complex apps, Base "
"simplifies inheritance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:29
msgid ""
"**Easy to test**: No special setup should be required to unit test `Base`"
" or base plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:31
msgid "Minimal API surface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/base_README.md:33
msgid ""
"[The API](#api) was designed to provide only the minimum necessary "
"functionality for creating a useful application, with or without "
"[plugins](#plugins)."
msgstr ""

